  "body": "## Summary\n\nUpdates the installed Sepo agent infrastructure from **0.3.1** to **v0.4.0** (`df515121bbc9e9d0e066642df57ac6075b90ee8f`).\n\n- **Source:** `self-evolving/repo` @ `v0.4.0` (SHA `df515121bbc9e9d0e066642df57ac6075b90ee8f`, resolution: latest-release)\n- **Target branch:** `agent/update-agent-infra-20260701` (base `main`)\n- **Scope:** `.agent/` (69 files) and `.github/` (23 files) — 92 files changed, no files outside agent-owned infrastructure\n\n### Notable upstream changes in 0.4.0\n- Live progress comments for implement/fix-PR runs, with thumbs-down cancellation.\n- New `/add-rubrics` route (draft PRs against `agent/rubrics`).\n- `download-github-attachment` CLI for private attachments.\n- Bundled `.agent/model-defaults.json` provider defaults.\n- Lane-based `.agent` test scripts (runtime / workflow / docs / shell).\n- ACPX date-pinned `claude-*` model fix and progress-reporting robustness fixes.\n\n## Audit summary\n\nThis install carries **literature-specific customizations inside the agent-owned tree**, so a blind overwrite was not safe. Files were classified against the pristine 0.3.1 baseline and merged accordingly:\n\n| Action | Files |\n|---|---|\n| Take upstream (no local customization) | most `.agent/src`, `.agent/docs`, all changed `.github` workflows/prompts, `run-agent-task/action.yml` |\n| Add new (0.4.0) | `progress-*`, `env.ts`, `actor-association.ts`, `github-attachment-download.ts`, `download-github-attachment.ts`, `cli/progress/`, local-runner `hooks/`, prompt `agent-add-rubrics.md` |\n| 3-way merge (target customization + upstream) | `.agent/src/github.ts` (literature deployment helpers), `.agent/src/acpx-adapter.ts`, `.agent/src/__tests__/acpx-adapter.test.ts`, `.agent/docs/customization/configuration-list.md`, `.agent/docs/index.md`, `.agent/package.json` (version bump only) |\n| Resolved to upstream superset | `.agent/src/__tests__/envelope.test.ts` (upstream includes the target's helper plus a new one) |\n| Keep target (upstream unchanged vs 0.3.1) | `.agent/src/discussion.ts` |\n| Preserve target customization | `.github/workflows/test-scripts.yml` (adds root Quartz `npm run check` / `npm run build` validation on top of the 0.4.0 agent check lanes) |\n\n### Customizations preserved (target-owned, untouched)\n- `.agent/src`: `literature-update.ts`, `cli/publish-literature-update.ts`, `cli/publish-preview-deployment.ts`, `cli/publish-canonical-deployment.ts`, `cli/inactivate-preview-deployments.ts`, and their tests\n- `.github/workflows`: `agent-add-paper.yml`, `agent-literature-daily.yml`, `agent-deploy-site-main.yml`, `agent-site-preview.yml`, `deploy.yml`\n- `.github/prompts`: `literature-add-paper.md`, `literature-daily.md`\n- `.github/actions`: `deploy-sepo-site`, `resolve-discussion-ids`, `resolve-agent-provider/package.json`\n- `.github`: `ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*`, `dependabot.yml`, `pull_request_template.md`\n- Root `.gitignore` already contained `.agent/dist/` and `.agent/node_modules/` — no change needed\n\n### Removed files\n- None (obsolete/legacy removal was disabled for this run).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `npm --prefix .agent ci` — OK\n- `npm --prefix .agent run build` (tsc) — OK (verified target literature CLIs compile against merged `github.ts`)\n- `npm --prefix .agent test` (build + runtime + workflow + docs + shell lanes) — **739 tests pass, 0 fail**\n- YAML parse of all 30 workflows + composite actions + action templates — OK\n- `git diff --check` and `git diff --cached --check` — clean\n\n## Branch status\n- `agent/memory` exists — will not be reinitialized.\n- `agent/rubrics` missing — optional; run `Agent / Rubrics / Initialization` only if the repo wants rubric steering.\n\n## Post-merge notes (document only)\n1. Verify provider/auth secrets still match the updated workflows.\n2. `agent/memory` already exists — rely on ongoing memory sync/scan workflows.\n3. Optionally initialize `agent/rubrics` if rubric steering is desired (enables the new `/add-rubrics` route end-to-end).\n4. Smoke-test with an issue mentioning `@sepo-agent /answer`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
